Object Ouputs - Using GExporter

    There are currently two supported formats for exporting Clados instances to flat text data. Neither is perfect in 
    the sense of conforming to type standards, but they are generally close.

    *   XML format is the older way. GExporter has a set of static methods that accept cladosG objects and an 'indentation'
        hint. The original idea was to provide each object with a static method to export itself, but in physical models
        with a lot of objects that seems like a waste of memory. The v2.0 way is to pile all of the methods in GExporter.

    *   JSON format is the newer way. GExporter doesn't have methods for exporting every type of cladosG object this way
        just yet... but will. I think the JSON exports will be a little smaller than XML exports, but that remains to 
        be seen.
    
    []

* Geometry Infrastructure

** Generators

    Generators don't have explicit XML or JSON output methods. They are all from the cladosG.Generator enumeration class,
    so one can simply call generator.toString() on them to get their text representation or generator.ord to get the byte int.

** Blades

    Blades are mostly an array of generators expressed in comma separated strings or byte int's. Blade in cladosG also 
    tracks two keys, though, so they also get exported. Blade's bit key is most likely familiar to geometric algebra 
    developers. Blade's other key is a long int than can distiguish two equivalent blades belonging to bases with 
    different sized pscalars.

+----------------------
Generators can be exported as byte integers instead.

XML
<Blade key="81985529216486896" bitKey="0b111111111111111" generators="E1,E2,E3,E4,E5,E6,E7,E8,E9,EA,EB,EC,ED,EE,EF" />
------
JSON
{
"blade": {
    "key": 81985529216486895, 
    "bitKey": "0b111111111111111",
    "generators": ["E1","E2","E3","E4","E5","E6","E7","E8","E9","EA","EB","EC","ED","EE","EF"]
    }
}

+----------------------

** Bases

    A Basis is mostly an array of Blades but stored as a list and sorted by Blade's key. The smallest key corresponds
    to the scalar blade while the largest key indicates the pscalar blade.

    Basis also tracks an array of list locations where blades of a particular grade are found. This is about cycle
    management because a lot of typical uses for multivectors do not populate all the grades equally. Rather than
    compute blade ranges every time they are needed, they are stored in Basis.

    Finally, Basis also tracks a UUID to assist with memory management efforts that recognize that Basis has no signature 
    information. This makes every basis using the same number of generators internally identical suggesting references
    to bases stored in a cache would suffice in many problems. (Signature shows up in the geometric product class.)
    This use of UUID may change in the near future, though, since the pscalar's key is smaller and should suffice.

+----------------------
Generators can be exported as byte integers instead.

XML
<Basis UUID="cb77eeff-fe96-4645-add3-13c709de3691">
	<Grades count="5">
		<Grade rank="0" range="0-0" />
		<Grade rank="1" range="1-4" />
		<Grade rank="2" range="5-10" />
		<Grade rank="3" range="11-14" />
		<Grade rank="4" range="15-15" />
	</Grades>
	<Blades count="16">
		<Blade key="0"   bitKey="0b0000" generators="           " />
		<Blade key="1"   bitKey="0b0001" generators="E1         " />
		<Blade key="2"   bitKey="0b0010" generators="   E2      " />
		<Blade key="3"   bitKey="0b0100" generators="      E3   " />
		<Blade key="4"   bitKey="0b1000" generators="         E4" />
		<Blade key="7"   bitKey="0b0011" generators="E1,E2      " />
		<Blade key="8"   bitKey="0b0101" generators="E1,   E3   " />
		<Blade key="9"   bitKey="0b1001" generators="E1,      E4" />
		<Blade key="13"  bitKey="0b0110" generators="   E2,E3   " />
		<Blade key="14"  bitKey="0b1010" generators="   E2,   E4" />
		<Blade key="19"  bitKey="0b1100" generators="      E3,E4" />
		<Blade key="38"  bitKey="0b0111" generators="E1,E2,E3   " />
		<Blade key="39"  bitKey="0b1011" generators="E1,E2,   E4" />
		<Blade key="44"  bitKey="0b1101" generators="E1,   E3,E4" />
		<Blade key="69"  bitKey="0b1110" generators="   E2,E3,E4" />
		<Blade key="194" bitKey="0b1111" generators="E1,E2,E3,E4" />
	</Blades>
</Basis>
------
JSON
{
"basis": {
	"UUID": "ae411b73-e758-4f1b-a00f-4a1ca8feae5f", 
	"Grades": {
		"count": 5, 
		"grade": [	{"rank": 0, "range": "0-0"}, 
				{"rank": 1, "range": "1-4"}, 
				{"rank": 2, "range": "5-10"}, 
				{"rank": 3, "range": "11-14"}, 
				{"rank": 4, "range": "15-15"}]
		}, 
	"Blades": {
		"count": 16, 
		"blade": [ 	{"key": 0, "bitKey": "0b0000", "generators": []}, 
				{"key": 1, "bitKey": "0b0001", "generators": ["E1"]}, 
				{"key": 2, "bitKey": "0b0010", "generators": ["E2"]}, 
				{"key": 3, "bitKey": "0b0100", "generators": ["E3"]}, 
				{"key": 4, "bitKey": "0b1000", "generators": ["E4"]}, 
				{"key": 7, "bitKey": "0b0011", "generators": ["E1","E2"]}, 
				{"key": 8, "bitKey": "0b0101", "generators": ["E1","E3"]}, 
				{"key": 9, "bitKey": "0b1001", "generators": ["E1","E4"]}, 
				{"key": 13, "bitKey": "0b0110", "generators": ["E2","E3"]}, 
				{"key": 14, "bitKey": "0b1010", "generators": ["E2","E4"]}, 
				{"key": 19, "bitKey": "0b1100", "generators": ["E3","E4"]}, 
				{"key": 38, "bitKey": "0b0111", "generators": ["E1","E2","E3"]}, 
				{"key": 39, "bitKey": "0b1011", "generators": ["E1","E2","E4"]}, 
				{"key": 44, "bitKey": "0b1101", "generators": ["E1","E3","E4"]}, 
				{"key": 69, "bitKey": "0b1110", "generators": ["E2","E3","E4"]}, 
				{"key": 194, "bitKey": "0b1111", "generators": ["E1","E2","E3","E4"]} ]
		}
	}
}

